                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Not actively bad but average at best. The writing is passable but the scenario is kind of shallow and the fantasy elements do not really add anything to the theme of self and social acceptance. Many of the characters look like there is something wrong with their necks or like their faces were pasted onto existing illustrations. I have no idea what the note Eiko reads in the ending is about. I guess it is something from the developer and I am just unaware of whatever real-life drama inspired it. I am cutting the developer a little slack here because this appears to be their first work but while the game is not bad enough to actively advise people against buying it, it does not really have anything that makes it worth recommending.",
